  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-027 (amended) + T225a adr-check F2">
      Do NOT change `ArmDeploymentRunner`'s Model 1 arm — it keeps failing closed (`arm-template-unavailable`) until T228
      brings per-customer subscriptions; T228 flips it. Do not remove the ISH-02 Model 1 subscription exemption (T228).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/provisioning.md § KV credential lifecycle (BINDING)">
      No live Key Vault write, delete or purge in this task. Never create, seed or restore `BFF-API-ClientSecret` (either
      casing) or `Dataverse-ClientSecret` in a secret-free environment. In `Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1` change ONLY the
      `AzureOpenAI-Endpoint` entry and the header/example count drift — do not touch the `Dataverse-ClientSecret`,
      `BFF-API-ClientSecret`, `Sidecar-Shared-Secret`, `Exchange-Connect-Cert` or `Redis-ConnectionString` entries.
      `SecretFreeIdentityRollback` semantics stay as they are.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D18 (2026-10-02)">
      Remove `BingSearch-ApiKey` and `LlamaParse-ApiKey` from `scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml` and
      regenerate every generated output with the generator (never hand-edit generated files). If, after the removal, no
      manifest entry uses `value_source: from-platform-vault`, remove that value source end to end: the resolver branch,
      the H4 writer's vendor-key pre-write check, `KvSecretsPopulationOptions.PlatformVaultName` + its boot validation,
      the manifest schema enum value, and the Worker Bicep `vendorKeysKeyVaultName` param + its
      `KvSecretsPopulationOptions__PlatformVaultName` setting (a required boot option nothing reads is a failure mode).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="plan G6 + INCOMING §5 Item 3">
      Pairing after this task: `Model1` ↔ `spaarke-hosted-model2`; `Model2` ↔ `customer-owned-model2`. Every other pair is
      refused with the existing invalid-pair error code; `spaarke-hosted-model1-trial` is retired from the known profile
      set (refused as an unknown profile). Do NOT
      rename the profile vocabulary (out of scope — record a one-line follow-up for T235 if you think it should be).
      Record the change as an extension of the T245a ADR-020 row in spec.md ADR Tensions (same callers, same reasoning).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10 / project scope">
      No change to `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api` (the BFF's dead Bing v7 code is on the BFF follow-up list).
      `controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep` untouched (T228). `H0Options.RequireCostEnvelopeForModel2Dedicated` /
      `isModel2Dedicated` are T229 — do not rename them here.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="Sub-agent write boundary">
      `.claude/**` edits (provision-environment skill prose, CHANGELOG, constraints/patterns if they name a removed option)
      are made by the main session.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>`SharedPlatformSearchEndpoint`, the tenant-filter template provisioner or `SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint` has a consumer that is not the Model 1 branch → STOP and report before deleting it.</trigger>
    <trigger>Making secret-free the default would change the behaviour of a run against an existing live environment (e.g. the prong-3 `spaarkedev1` exception, sunset 2026-11-23) → STOP; do not work around it with a new flag.</trigger>
    <trigger>Removing the `from-platform-vault` value source would require a change outside the control plane, the catalog generator, its schema and the Worker Bicep (e.g. the BFF) → STOP; keep the mechanism, make `PlatformVaultName` optional, and record why.</trigger>
    <trigger>The registry (`sprk_dataverseenvironment`) or any stored artifact carries profile values the new pairing would orphan → STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Confirm the branch is 0 behind origin/master (re-merge if not). `git grep -n` for `SharedPlatformSearchEndpoint`, `SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint`, `TenantFilterTemplate`, `spaarke-hosted-model1-trial`, `Model1Shared`, `BingSearch`, `LlamaParse`, `from-platform-vault`, `PlatformVaultName`, `vendorKeysKeyVaultName` → categorized hit list in the POML notes.</step>
