  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Model 1 run, H2b creates indexes on the AI Search endpoint H2a produced, through the same code path as Model 2; given that output is absent, it fails with the same rejection code Model 2 uses. No `HandleModel1BranchAsync`, `SharedPlatformSearchEndpoint` or tenant-filter template provisioner remains in code, DI, Worker config or Bicep.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Model 1 run, H12c's OpenAI runtime reference is the stamp's own endpoint; no `SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint` remains in code, Worker config, Bicep (incl. compiled JSON) or `Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`POST /api/runs` accepts `Model1`+`spaarke-hosted-model2` and `Model2`+`customer-owned-model2`; it refuses `Model1`+`customer-owned-model2` and `Model2`+`spaarke-hosted-model2` with the existing invalid-pair code, and `spaarke-hosted-model1-trial` (retired from the known profile set) with the existing unknown-profile code; `intake.schema.json` agrees (schema/endpoint parity test passes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With default options, H4 writes neither `Dataverse-ClientSecret` nor `BFF-API-ClientSecret`; the Worker Bicep sets `KvSecretsPopulationOptions__RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`; `PinnedManifestGaps` contains only the T246 and T227 pins; existing rollback tests pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The canonical secret catalog has no `BingSearch-ApiKey` or `LlamaParse-ApiKey`; generated files match the generator (`-Verify` OK); either the `from-platform-vault` mechanism and `PlatformVaultName` are gone end to end, or (escalation 3) the option is optional and the reason is recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No file or type name in src/ contains `Model1Shared`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`ArmDeploymentRunner`'s Model 1 arm still throws (its T2 test unchanged); `controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep` and `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api` unchanged; no live Key Vault operation performed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ControlPlane projects build 0/0; ControlPlane.Tests has no failures beyond the 6 T221 baseline; ArchTests pass; `bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` PASS; prereqs `validate.ps1` OK.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the changed contracts and the negative cases named in these criteria. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the POML notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Filed 2026-10-02 from plan §7 T225b + owner D18. Scope change vs the plan row: the ArmDeploymentRunner Model 1 → `customer`
    flip moved to T228 (flipping it before per-customer subscriptions exist would deploy a full stamp into a shared
    subscription — T225a adr-check F2 / ADR-027).

    COMPLETION (2026-10-02). Verified: ControlPlane Api / Worker / Tests / LoadTests build 0 warnings 0 errors;
    ControlPlane.Tests 2124 pass / 6 fail (the T221 CustomerRunGuardModulePostConfigureTests baseline) / 1 skip;
    ArchTests 340/340; bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1 OVERALL PASS; prereqs validate.ps1 OK (34 prereqs, manifest v5); catalog
    -Verify OK; customer.json + platform-controlplane.json = fresh compiles (`--outfile`); Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1
    binds all 10 parameters (Get-Command).

    DONE: H2b + H13's I2 probe + H12c run one path for both models on the stamp's own AI Search / OpenAI (deleted:
    HandleModel1BranchAsync, AiSearchIndexOptions.SharedPlatformSearchEndpoint, the Cosmos tenant-filter template store
    + provisioner + tests, RuntimeReferencesOptions.SharedPlatformOpenAiEndpoint, its Worker Bicep KV ref +
    azureOpenAiEndpointSecretName params, the Seed-PlatformKeyVault AzureOpenAI-Endpoint entry, 3 rejection codes:
    shared-index-missing, tenant-filter-template-provision-failed, runtimerefs-missing-shared-platform-endpoint-
    configuration — no documented consumer). G6 pairing (agent): Model1↔spaarke-hosted-model2, Model2↔customer-owned-
    model2, trial profile retired (refused `tenancy-profile-invalid`); schema allOf pinned against the endpoint by a new
    parity test. G13: TenancyModelDagParityTests. G21: KvSecretsPopulationOptions.RequireSecretFreeIdentity = true by
    default + Worker Bicep sets it; SecretFreeIdentityOmitTargets = {BFF-API-ClientSecret, Dataverse-ClientSecret}
    (owner-approved binding rule — resolution record decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md lines
    168/174: never CREATE either in a secret-free env; rule 2's hold protects the EXISTING copy from deletion only);
    both PinnedManifestGaps removed; customer.bicep's dead requireSecretFreeIdentity param removed with its intake key,
    H2a read, BicepDeployRequest field and runner payload entry (the param's own description said "removal paired with
    the runner change (T225b)"). D18 (agent): BingSearch-ApiKey + LlamaParse-ApiKey + the from-platform-vault source
    removed end to end (generator, C#, options, Worker Bicep `vendorKeysKeyVaultName`, tests; enum slot 9 tombstoned —
    not persisted anywhere, adr-check verified); generated files regenerated.

    ESCALATION TRIGGERS: (1) the tenant-filter template store had a 2nd consumer, H13's I2 probe — but it was the I2
    probe's MODEL 1 branch, i.e. the same retired shared-tier logic, so the trigger (a consumer that is NOT the Model 1
    branch) did not fire; converging it here instead of in T230 kept H13 from failing every Model 1 run (deviation:
    pulled forward from T230; plan T230 row + G5 updated). (2) Secret-free default changes no live environment's runs:
    H4 only ever writes NEW stamps' vaults; prong 3 is spaarkedev1 only. (3) from-platform-vault removal needed nothing
    outside the control plane / catalog / Worker Bicep (BFF keeps its own Bing config — follow-up). (4) Profile values:
    only the intake template carried the trial profile (updated); stored runs are never re-validated, and pre-T224 runs
    carry "Model1Shared", already unparseable — so no resumable Model 1 run can hit the converged H2b path (adr-check W6).

    QUALITY GATES (Step 9.5): code-review — C1 Critical FIXED (Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1: removing $AzureOpenAiEndpoint
    left a stray [Parameter] attribute, the script would not bind; my earlier check only parsed it); W1 FIXED at source
    (secret-free default ⇒ H4 always writes the A38a marker to registry column sprk_credentialmode, which does NOT exist
    on spaarkedev1 — read-only check 2026-10-02: added to the idempotent Extend-DataverseEnvironmentSchema-v3.3.ps1 +
    new prerequisite PRQ-E-14; LIVE creation awaits owner approval); W2 rollback scope documented on the option; W3/adr
    W2 rollout order recorded below; W4 spec ADR-038 row renamed; W5 inventory/plan I2 rows; W6 pairing parity test
    added; S1 replaced my H2a "removed field absent" test with a real check — every BuildParametersPayload key is
    declared in customer.json (ArmTemplateInspectorTests); S2 explicit legacy options; S3 skill tenancy check case-
